---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { appleEulaUrl, supportEmail } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Quiet Poker — Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that apply to Quiet Poker: Apple's standard licence agreement, plus what the play chips are and are not."
  prose
>
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>

  <p>
    Quiet Poker is licensed, not sold, under Apple&rsquo;s
    <a href={appleEulaUrl}>Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a>,
    the standard agreement that applies to apps downloaded from the App Store.
    Downloading or using the app means accepting it.
  </p>

  <p>
    There is no second agreement. The notes below describe the app; where they
    could ever be read as conflicting with Apple&rsquo;s agreement, Apple&rsquo;s
    agreement is what applies.
  </p>

  <h2>What the chips are</h2>
  <p>
    The chips in Quiet Poker are play chips. They have no cash value and no
    value of any kind outside the app. They cannot be cashed out, sold,
    redeemed, exchanged, transferred to another player, or wagered on anything.
    Buying a chip pack buys chips to keep playing with; it does not buy a stake,
    a balance, or a claim on anything.
  </p>

  <p>
    This game is intended for an adult audience. This game does not offer
    real-money gambling or an opportunity to win real money or prizes. Practice
    or success in this game does not imply future success at real-money
    gambling.
  </p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Chip packs and the Plus subscription are sold by Apple through the App
    Store, in your own currency, at the price shown in the app&rsquo;s Shop tab
    at the time of purchase. Payment, refunds, billing questions and
    cancellation are handled by Apple under the terms of your App Store account.
  </p>

  <p>
    A Plus subscription renews until you cancel it. Cancel from Settings on your
    iPhone, or from Manage subscription in the Shop tab. Cancelling stops the
    next renewal; the paid period you are in runs to its end.
  </p>

  <p>
    Chips already credited stay credited. Chips are not refundable by us,
    because we never took the payment &mdash; a refund is a matter between you
    and Apple.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair play</h2>
  <p>
    Online tables rely on every seat running an unmodified copy of the app. An
    account used to tamper with results, to automate play, or to disrupt other
    players&rsquo; games may lose access to online play.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can play offline without an account. If you sign in with Apple, you can
    delete the account and its chips from the Profile tab at any time. What that
    removes is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The app is provided as it is</h2>
  <p>
    Quiet Poker is provided without warranty of any kind, to the extent the law
    allows. It is a game; it is not advice, and nothing in it is a prediction of
    anything outside it.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
